    "body": "The computation-only observation/intent fit omitted correction, nonassertion, project relations and historical questions. Fit one combined support set and build primary worlds through actual learned observation/ingestion. The same candidate now retains38/38 prior outcomes and37/37 ingests; the narrow ablation reproduces17/38. Signed finite computation is retained, with an ordinary finite table tying its answers.\n\nPrincipal review independently reconstructs392 outcomes,649selected records and338emissions, verifies all four19-file seals, and corrects primary ingestion to72/72. The32-case added panel first passes in attempt2; attempt4 is an exposed replay. Typed comparison counters are scoped as reported because individual typed traces were not saved. Grounding and consumption are atomic; no nonexistent intermediate checkpoint is claimed.\n\nAdded test-only loaded-artifact checks cover corrections to actual operands/downstream records and same-payload role changes.42parent+42child full-frame restores retain the pinned old answer while fresh answers change.479priorprimary/control rows match with explicit artifact-binding/view-hash exclusions. Production and learned parameters are unchanged by principal verification.\n\nThe updated canonical roadmap and full execution brief direct learned grounded lexical realization: Copy/Vocabulary/Stop plus an evidence-dependent vocabulary effect, using E/S as a local donor. This does not claim general prose, a learned general scheduler, geometric superiority, full-path D0-b or energy savings.\n\nValidation: release runner test build;25standard tests pass,4explicitly ignored by default;2artifact-dependent parent tests explicitly pass with3child processes; format, claim wording, JSON and local document-target checks pass. Original submitted27scoped+23observed-text module test logs are retained. Reported other library-test failures lack a reproduced parent baseline and remain unattributed. Resource accounting is reconciled; unique artifacts preserved; no paid compute.\n\nReferences #820, #973, #1139, #962, #963, #964.\n",
