      "body": "Follow-up commit `8430664c` (docs/evidence only; the bound harness source `b2245a4d…` is unchanged):\n\n- the separate-process restart replays **ten** checkpoint phases — `Read`, three `Apply`, `Read`, three `Emit`, two `Stop` — and every one reproduces the complete final frame. That makes the brief's four save/reload points explicit rather than inferred: before the computation starts, during a nonempty operation sequence (after each applied operation), after grounding and before consumption, and after the later source capture.\n- the evidence receipt gains a `saved_state_restore` section and still reports **zero** discrepancies between the independent reconstruction and the harness summary.\n\nNo measured number in the PR description changes.\n",
